garrett (1.3.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * The privacy shield no longer holds up the part of the agent that stops
    attacks while it writes its firewall entries. In 1.3.0 an attack that
    started at that moment could get through.
  * macOS: switching the shield off removes every route the agent added.
  * A garrett command whose output is piped into another program ends
    quietly when that program stops reading.

 -- sentinels <noreply@sentinels.invalid>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0000

garrett (1.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * The privacy shield, on unless switched off (SHIELD=off). It notes which
    program on the machine talks to which advertising and tracking network,
    and keeps that record on the machine ("garrett traffic").
  * After the settling-in day a tracker is refused at the firewall when it
    answers from a network of its own company and no program other than a
    browser uses it here. A tracker that shares its addresses with sites
    people visit is measured and never refused. No setting of the operating
    system is changed.
  * New commands: "garrett shield" (what is refused, what is left open and
    why; on, off, allow <name>, cut <name>) and "garrett traffic".

 -- sentinels <noreply@sentinels.invalid>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000

garrett (1.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * A fresh install settles in for a day (LEARN_HOURS). What is plainly an
    attack is stopped from the first second; a program that only its score
    speaks against is reported and left running until its owner judges it.
  * On a machine with no service, garrett learns from its owner's verdicts:
    signals they keep calling theirs count for less, ones they keep
    confirming count for more, and two signals that confirmed attacks share
    become a sign of attack there. No model is involved.
  * New commands: "garrett confirm <case>" (that was an attack) and
    "garrett learned" (what this machine has learned; --reset forgets it).

 -- sentinels <noreply@sentinels.invalid>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000

garrett (1.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * First release from the sentinels repository.
  * The agent keeps itself current: it installs each new version by
    itself, after checking the project's signature on it. UPDATE=off in
    /etc/garrett/garrett.conf turns that off. "garrett update" does it now.
  * Linux: a burst of failed SSH sign-ins from one address is reported.
  * Windows: startup entries that appear while the agent watches are judged,
    and switched off when they run what an intruder would.
  * A service that calls back the address that attacked it has that one
    address refused for an hour.
  * Windows: the agent no longer takes its own Security-log lookup for an
    attack.

